Subject: [PATCH 4/4] MIG-1 F-B: Primitives specs, forwarding map, pair
 duplication via pairDiagTM

Fill Turing.FinTM.polyUnaryTM_spaceUsed (with the head invariant
polyHeads / poly_step / poly_space moved from Catalog's f2_ copies; the
trajectory bound uses workTapePos_runFrom_mem_Icc and
spaceUsedByTape_le_card_Icc), unaryTokenTM_computes and
appendBitTM_computes (row bodies moved; computesFunInTime_unaryToken and
computesFunInTime_appendBit are corollaries).

Add the three gated forwarding exports Turing.FinTM.pairMapSndTM,
pairMapSndTM_computes (coefficient 22) and pairMapSndTM_spaceUsed (payload
coefficient one). The witness is Catalog's forwarding controller
(a2_mapTM Mg true), moved here with its private implementation and renamed
fwdMap*; its private Fin-sum equivalence is replaced by Fin.sum_univ_add.
computesFunInTime_pairMapSnd is re-pointed to pairMapSndTM; the old
captured-output controller (pairMapTM, mapCfg ... pairMap_computes) and the
then-unused catalogPayload_computes are retired. computesFunInTime_pairDup
now uses Turing.pairDiagTM; the private pairDupTM family is retired.
